comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T00:19:58.543Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all-status PM items for stdin-json and notes; closed pm-kipd delivered the original round-trip feature and pm-a2h3 delivered direct note editing, but neither tracks this new silent no-op defect. GitHub issue #1343 has no prior PM link."
  "2026-09-29T04:56:30.520Z","harness:codex","Test-audit contract: a changed persisted note in get->modify->update --stdin-json must never return a successful no-op. Existing structured round-trip test only appends a new note and does not detect edits to a persisted annotation. Primary proof will use a disposable tracker and history verification; no test-only production seam."
  "2026-09-29T06:50:36.685Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: full-item get to update --stdin-json now preserves persisted comments, notes, and learnings as immutable snapshots and rejects edited or removed entries under the item lock with stdin_json_persisted_annotation_changed. The structured-mutation integration test proves the formerly silent edited-note no-op fails without changing item or history, while legitimate new annotations still append. Linked test passed; full suite 9414 passed; exact V8 coverage 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passed. Manual correction remains pm notes/comments/learnings --edit with audit history."
  "2026-09-29T07:17:18.050Z","harness:codex","PR #1348 review follow-up: malformed full-item annotation arrays now return a PM usage error instead of an unhandled TypeError. Focused parser tests cover all three annotation fields with user-visible diagnostics; these exercise an independent invalid-input boundary rather than mirroring the implementation."
  "2026-09-29T07:42:04.396Z","harness:codex","Correction to prior review note: the existing appendFacetOptions -> serializeObjectArray path already refuses null comments/notes/learnings with a field-specific PmCliError before the persisted-snapshot filter. The suggested extra guard was unreachable and failed the exact 100% coverage gate, so it was removed. New regression assertions verify the existing usage code and field guidance on all three inputs; no production behavior change was needed for this bot finding."
  "2026-09-29T08:09:24.273Z","harness:codex","Final PR #1348 review verification: all 9414 tests passed, exact V8 coverage is 100/100/100/100, pnpm quality:static and pnpm security:scan passed, and both linked structured-mutation integration and parser unit tests passed through pm test in an isolated schema tracker. Null annotation arrays produce the existing typed usage refusal; the extra guard suggested in review was removed as unreachable."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T06:50:37.375Z","harness:codex","A full-item JSON round trip must distinguish new annotation entries from persisted audit entries and verify the persisted snapshot inside the locked mutation, including annotation-only updates."
